 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Registration is a two-phase record-and-replay. All paths are under `src/tessel/`.\n\n**1. Recording (before registration)**\n- `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (`sansio/bundles.py:413`) doesn't touch an app. It calls `self.record(...)` (`:433`) with a deferred lambda that invokes `state.attach_route_rule(...)`.\n- `Bundle.record` (`sansio/bundles.py:224`) appends that lambda to `Bundle.deferred_functions`.\n\n**2. Registration**\n- `Tessel.register_bundle` (`sansio/app.py:571`) calls `bundle.register(self, options)`.\n- `Bundle.register` (`sansio/bundles.py:273`) does the following:\n  - It records the bundle in `app.bundles`.\n  - It calls `make_setup_state` (`:246`) to build a `BundleSetupState`.\n  - It adds the static route via `state.attach_route_rule` if `has_static_folder` is set (`:323`).\n  - It replays every deferred function with the state (`:334`).\n  - It recurses into nested bundles, composing `url_prefix` and `subdomain` (`:349`).\n\n**3. Applying rules to the app**\n- `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`sansio/bundles.py:87`) does the following:\n  - It applies the `url_prefix` and `subdomain`.\n  - It merges the `url_defaults`.\n  - It prefixes the endpoint with `name_prefix.name.`.\n  - It calls `app.attach_route_rule`.\n- `App.attach_route_rule` (`sansio/app.py:606`) adds the rule to the app's URL map.",
